    ('muslim@csc.tcd.ie', 'en', '{"sujet": "When a child can’t get a place at your madrasah", "corps": "Assalamu alaykum wa rahmatullah,\n\nYour madrasah teaches the Qur’an in person, and that is the best way whenever it is possible. But you will know families who can’t make it: the classes are full, the evening times clash with work or school, or they live too far away.\n\nRewayah Academy is there for them: live online Qur’an classes in small groups, with the same teacher three times a week. We don’t replace your madrasah; we reach the children it can’t.\n\nIf a family comes to mind, simply pass on this link:\nhttps://rewayahacademy.com/en/familles?ref=trinity-college-dublin-muslim\n\nThe Prophet ﷺ said: “The one who guides to good is like the one who does it.” (at-Tirmidhi)\n\nJazakAllahu khayran,\nAbdoulaye Mouhidine Sow\nDirector, Rewayah Academy", "langue_source": "en", "raison": "You are receiving this message because your organisation teaches the Qur’an and says so publicly.", "campagne": "prospection-v3", "type": "lettre", "segment": "en_uk", "temoin_sans_image": false, "image": {"src": "https://rewayahacademy.com/fr/assets/courriel-prospection-en.png", "alt": "For the students who cannot come. “The one who guides to good is like the one who does it.” Hadith narrated by at-Tirmidhi, no. 2670. Rewayah Academy.", "largeur": 600, "hauteur": 315}}'::jsonb, '2026-11-30T10:18:05+00:00'::timestamptz, 'prospection-v3:muslim@csc.tcd.ie'),
